 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🚀 ETL Pipeline Dashboard\n",
    "\n",
    "## Monitor ETL Run History and Performance\n",
    "\n",
    "This dashboard shows:\n",
    "- **Recent ETL runs** with success/failure status\n",
    "- **Manual vs CRON** run detection\n",
    "- **Performance metrics** (videos processed, duration)\n",
    "- **Error tracking** and failure reasons\n",
    "- **Success rates** by channel and time period\n",
    "\n",
    "Perfect for monitoring your daily ETL pipeline and troubleshooting issues."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📊 ETL Dashboard Setup\n",
    "# Setup Python path for imports\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.abspath(\'.\'))\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.abspath(\'../..\'))\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "from web.etl_helpers import get_engine, get_etl_run_summary\n",
    "from sqlalchemy import text\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🚀 ETL Dashboard loaded successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📋 Recent ETL Runs (Last 7 Days)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📊 Load recent ETL run data\n",
    "print(\"📊 Loading ETL run history...\")\n",
    "runs_df = get_etl_run_summary(days=7)\n",
    "\n",
    "if not runs_df.empty:\n",
    "    print(f\"📈 Found {len(runs_df)} ETL runs in the last 7 days\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Format for display\n",
    "    display_df = runs_df.copy()\n",
    "    display_df['duration_minutes'] = (display_df['duration_seconds'] / 60).round(2)\n",
    "    display_df['started_at'] = pd.to_datetime(display_df['started_at']).dt.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Show key columns\n",
    "    cols_to_show = ['channel_id', 'run_date', 'started_at', 'status', 'run_type', \n",
    "                   'videos_processed', 'metrics_collected', 'duration_minutes']\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"\\n🏆 RECENT ETL RUNS:\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "    display(display_df[cols_to_show])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Show any errors\n",
    "    errors = runs_df[runs_df['status'] == 'failed']\n",
    "    if not errors.empty:\n",
    "        print(\"\\n❌ FAILED RUNS:\")\n",
    "        for _, row in errors.iterrows():\n",
    "            print(f\"   {row['channel_id']} ({row['run_date']}): {row['error_message']}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"📭 No ETL runs found in the last 7 days\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📊 ETL Performance Summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📊 Calculate performance metrics\n",
    "if not runs_df.empty:\n",
    "    print(\"📊 ETL PERFORMANCE SUMMARY:\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Overall stats\n",
    "    total_runs = len(runs_df)\n",
    "    successful_runs = len(runs_df[runs_df['status'] == 'success'])\n",
    "    failed_runs = len(runs_df[runs_df['status'] == 'failed'])\n",
    "    success_rate = (successful_runs / total_runs * 100) if total_runs > 0 else 0\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"📈 Total Runs: {total_runs}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ Successful: {successful_runs} ({success_rate:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "    print(f\"❌ Failed: {failed_runs}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Run type breakdown\n",
    "    manual_runs = len(runs_df[runs_df['run_type'] == 'manual'])\n",
    "    cron_runs = len(runs_df[runs_df['run_type'] == 'cron'])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\n🎯 RUN TYPE BREAKDOWN:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   👤 Manual: {manual_runs}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   🤖 CRON: {cron_runs}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Performance metrics\n",
    "    if successful_runs > 0:\n",
    "        successful_df = runs_df[runs_df['status'] == 'success']\n",
    "        avg_duration = successful_df['duration_seconds'].mean() / 60\n",
    "        total_videos = successful_df['videos_processed'].sum()\n",
    "        total_metrics = successful_df['metrics_collected'].sum()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        print(f\"\\n⚡ PERFORMANCE METRICS:\")\n",
    "        print(f\"   ⏱️ Avg Duration: {avg_duration:.1f} minutes\")\n",
    "        print(f\"   🎵 Total Videos Processed: {total_videos:,}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"   📊 Total Metrics Collected: {total_metrics:,}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Channel breakdown\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n🎤 BY CHANNEL:\")\n",
    "    channel_stats = runs_df.groupby('channel_id').agg({\n",
    "        'status': lambda x: (x == 'success').sum(),\n",
    "        'channel_id': 'count',\n",
    "        'videos_processed': 'sum',\n",
    "        'metrics_collected': 'sum'\n",
    "    }).rename(columns={'status': 'successful', 'channel_id': 'total_runs'})\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for channel, stats in channel_stats.iterrows():\n",
    "        success_pct = (stats['successful'] / stats['total_runs'] * 100) if stats['total_runs'] > 0 else 0\n",
    "        print(f\"   {channel}: {stats['successful']}/{stats['total_runs']} ({success_pct:.0f}%) - {stats['videos_processed']} videos, {stats['metrics_collected']} metrics\")\n",
    "\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"📭 No data available for performance summary\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔍 Detailed Error Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 🔍 Analyze errors and failures\n",
    "if not runs_df.empty:\n",
    "    failed_runs = runs_df[runs_df['status'] == 'failed']\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if not failed_runs.empty:\n",
    "        print(\"🔍 DETAILED ERROR ANALYSIS:\")\n",
    "        print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for _, run in failed_runs.iterrows():\n",
    "            print(f\"\\n❌ {run['channel_id']} - {run['run_date']} ({run['run_type']})\")\n",
    "            print(f\"   📝 Reason: {run['reason']}\")\n",
    "            print(f\"   💥 Error: {run['error_message']}\")\n",
    "            print(f\"   ⏱️ Duration: {run['duration_seconds']} seconds\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"✅ No failed runs in the last 7 days - great job!\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "    # Check for patterns\n",
    "    if len(failed_runs) > 1:\n",
    "        print(\"\\n🔍 FAILURE PATTERNS:\")\n",
    "        error_patterns = failed_runs['error_message'].value_counts()\n",
    "        for error, count in error_patterns.items():\n",
    "            if count > 1:\n",
    "                print(f\"   🔄 '{error}' occurred {count} times\")\n",
    "\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"📭 No error data available\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🎯 Recommendations\n",
    "\n",
    "Based on the ETL run analysis, here are some recommendations:\n",
    "\n",
    "### ✅ If Success Rate > 95%\n",
    "- Your ETL pipeline is running smoothly\n",
    "- Consider increasing data collection frequency if needed\n",
    "- Monitor for any performance degradation\n",
    "\n",
    "### ⚠️ If Success Rate 80-95%\n",
    "- Review failed runs for patterns\n",
    "- Check API quotas and rate limits\n",
    "- Consider adding retry logic for transient failures\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🔴 If Success Rate < 80%\n",
    "- Immediate attention required\n",
    "- Review error messages for root causes\n",
    "- Check database connectivity and API credentials\n",
    "- Consider pausing automated runs until issues are resolved\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🤖 CRON vs Manual Runs\n",
    "- CRON runs should be the majority for consistent data collection\n",
    "- Manual runs are good for testing and troubleshooting\n",
    "- If too many manual runs, consider improving automation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📅 Dashboard completion summary\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(f\"🚀 ETL DASHBOARD COMPLETE\")\n",
    "print(f\"🕐 Generated: {datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')}\")\n",
    "if not runs_df.empty:\n",
    "    print(f\"📊 Runs Analyzed: {len(runs_df)}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"📅 Date Range: {runs_df['run_date'].min()} to {runs_df['run_date'].max()}\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(\"\\n💡 Tip: Run this dashboard regularly to monitor ETL health!\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
